---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii1_79",
  "series": "Band II 1 (1663 - 1685)",
  "seq": 79,
  "text": "<p> [[213.14]] <b>67. LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY</p>\n<p> [[213.15]] [22. Juni 1671.] [66.70.]</b></p>\n<p> [[213.21]] Illustris et Ampl^#'m^#'e Vir </p>\n<p> [[213.22]] Mirabere me Tibi unis literis bis scribere, sed ita faciendi ratio fuit. Nam exteriores illas\n[[213.23]] apertas et Ill^#'m^#'o Gravellio inspiciendas reliqui. Sed has velut ab alio scriptas claudi amicus\n[[213.24]] jussit, cujus negotium propono. Negotium est maximi momenti dignumque cura tua, dignum\n[[214.1]] attentione Summi Viri Colberti vestri, cui etiam non ignotum est. Dⁿ^#'u^#'s Kraft Germanus,\n[[214.2]] Chymicus et Mechanicus in paucis eximius, et praeterea quod in eo genere rarum, prudens\n[[214.3]] catus et probus, per Germaniam principibus curiosisque aestimatus, idemque itineribus in\n[[214.4]] Indiam Occidentalem clarus, caeterum mihi in tanto licet experientiae discrimine, studiorum\n[[214.5]] quadam similitudine familiaris; is inquam Kraftius quod vulgo jam a tanto tempore jactatum\n[[214.6]] passimque etiam exiguis quibusdam speciminibus seu ut vocant probis, in magno tamen vel\n[[214.7]] non succedentibus, vel ob impensas infructuosis, adumbratum est, <b>mutationem ferri</b> <b>in\n[[214.8]] chalybem</i>, ad maximam perfectionem deduxit. Nam in magna copia chalybem parat, ipso\n[[214.9]] communi artificium consensu certissimisque testimoniis meliorem nec duritie tantum longissime\n[[214.10]] praecellentem, sed et tamen politurae quoque elaborationisque capacem. De fossili saepe\n[[214.11]] vix decem virgae dant unam bonam, harum artificialium fallit vix ulla. Quanti autem momenti\n[[214.12]] sit chalybs praesertim communi melior in Republica, quem recte <greek>^%)/organon ŏrgánvn</greek>, omniumque\n[[214.13]] belli pacisque artium instrumentum pene universale vocare liceat, nemo prudens non\n[[214.14]] videt. Sed rem privatis auspiciis occipere ausus non est, in Germania praesertim, chalybis\n[[214.15]] fodinas habente, exclamaturis non dominis tantum minerarum, sed et artificibus quibusdam et\n[[214.16]] mercatoribus, quorum circuli turbarentur. Ita enim comparatum est in Germania, ut praeter alias\n[[214.17]] causas conjecturatu faciles, tum vero ob opificum tribus legibus quibusdam saepe absurdis\n[[214.18]] vinctas, bona consilia, si nova, aegre exitum sortiantur, quibus malis vos unius domini vigor\n[[214.19]] facile absolvit. </p>\n<p> [[214.20]] Kraftio ergo aliquot abhinc annis ab Em^#'m^#'o Electore Moguntino in Galliam misso venit in\n[[214.21]] mentem rem Excellentissimo Colberto proponere, cujus nota ubique in procuranda Reipublicae\n[[214.22]] vestrae felicitate vigilantia cum maximo rerum pene omnium usu conjuncta, omnes facile,\n[[214.23]] praeclara molientes, allicit. Praesertim cum cogitaret Galliam non tantum chalybis sic satis\n[[214.24]] indigentem esse, sed et bona malaque sua egregie nosse; nec ad propositiones fructuosas\n[[214.25]] surdam esse. Colbertus, non tantum negotium recte cepit, sed et omni favore prosecutus est:\n[[214.26]] tractatum de transferenda in Galliam rei tam fructuosae tam longe alioquin petendae, officina;\n[[214.27]] consensum in privilegii designationem quandam (<i>project</i>) liberalissime amplissimeque extensam:\n[[214.28]] imo muneris Maximo Rege digni, quo nemo in egregiis minus parcus est, spes facta.\n[[214.29]] Interea nescio quomodo sufflaminatum est negotium[,] Kraftio rerum Moguntinarum causa,\n[[215.1]] incidente tum etiam Erphordiensi negotio, domum redire coacto, reque per absentiam ut solet,\n[[215.2]] refrigescente praesertim cum deesset Kraftio certus aliquis, cum quo in Gallia commercium\n[[215.3]] coleret, Ampl^#'m^#'o Dⁿ^#'o du Fraisne, continuante quidem et sustentante causam, sed ut fieri solet\n[[215.4]] itineribus et negotiis impedito interruptoque; Kraftio etiam (neque enim huic uni rei alligatus,\n[[215.5]] aut rei familiaris necessitate obstrictus est) compluribus interim jucundis fructuosisve experimentis\n[[215.6]] inventisque (quae hoc loco enumerare nihil attinet) tempus utiliter fallente. Sed cum\n[[215.7]] interea Dn. du Fraisne ad vos novissime reversus reassumtam rem scriberet, et vero jam annus\n[[215.8]] excesserit, ex quo aliunde oblatae sunt ejusdem negotii nomine conditiones valde speciosae,\n[[215.9]] quas neque rejecit, ne utrinque excideret, neque accepit, quod rem maxime Gallia dignam, a\n[[215.10]] Gallia optime prosequendam crederet: ideo putavit Kraftius moram omnem longiorem abrumpendam\n[[215.11]] sibi esse. Scripsit igitur Ampl^#'m^#'o Du Fraisnio responsionem decretoriam se jam tandem\n[[215.12]] avide expectare: diutius in suspenso manere non posse. Cumque intelligeret nonnullam mihi\n[[215.13]] Tecum, Vir illustris et Ampl^#'m^#'e notitiam intercedere, petiit ut primis ad Te literis hujus rei\n[[215.14]] mentionem facerem, stipulatus tamen silentii fidem, neque enim nisi quorum autoritate ad\n[[215.15]] exitum perduci debet, nosse necesse est. Sperat efficacius agi, quod duo separati urgeant. Quare\n[[215.16]] si hujus rei causa cum Summo Viro Colberto vestro ages, non Kraftium tantum maximo\n[[215.17]] beneficio Tibi obstringes, sed me quoque hac promtitudine humanitatis plurimum Tibi obligabis,\n[[215.18]] praesertim si quam fieri maturrime potest, rescribere digneris literasque non Herbipolin\n[[215.19]] nunc quidem ad Ill^#'m^#'u^#'m Gravellium, id enim ambagiosum est, sed recta Moguntiam dirigas,\n[[215.20]] modo literis mihi prius inscriptis obsignatisque hoc novum operculum circumdes: <i>A Monsieur\n[[215.21]] Monsieur Lasser, Conseiller de Son Altesse Electorale de Mayence. à Mayence.</i> Ita enim\n[[215.22]] certissime citissimeque ad me pervenient. Spero accepisse Te literas meas secundas, quas Dⁿ^#'o\n[[215.23]] Lersnero juveni erudito Senatoris Francfurtensis filio ad Vos eunti credidi, iis inserueram\n[[215.24]] Schedulam de re quadam non contemnenda, quam si accepisti legistique, rogo uti responso\n[[215.25]] quod proxime expecto aliam schedulam schedulae illi respondentem inseras. Quod superest\n[[215.26]] vale faveque et quamprimum rescribere dignare </p>\n<p> [[215.27]] Illustris et Ampl^#'m^#'e Vir, Cultori nominis famaeque Tuae devotissimo </p>\n<p> [[215.28]] G. G. Leibnitio. </p>\n",
  "number": "67.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY",
  "date": "[22. Juni 1671.] [66.70.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:67. LEIBNIZ FÜR PIERRE DE CARCAVY [22. Juni 1671.] [66.70.] Illustris et Ampl^#'m^#'e Vir Mirabere me Tibi unis literis bis scribere, sed ita faciendi ratio fuit. Nam exteriores illas apertas et Ill^#'m^#'o Gravellio inspiciendas reliqui. Sed has velut ab alio scriptas claudi amicus jussit, cujus ne...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>